{
  "uid": "gateway-overview",
  "title": "Self-Healing LLM Gateway",
  "description": "The demo arc, top to bottom: traffic reroutes, the circuit trips, errors and latency say why, and the queue absorbs what could not be served. Every query aggregates across the gateway and worker scrape jobs - both processes export the same collector names, so a query carrying a job label shows half the truth.",
  "tags": ["gateway", "llm"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "refresh": "5s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-15m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Traffic by provider, and what the caller got",
      "description": "The single most legible moment in the demo: when a provider is taken out, its band is replaced by the next rung's and the total line does not move. Bands are provider calls (stacked); the line is answers returned to callers, which is a different number - a request that failed over twice is three calls and one answer.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 16, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 70,
            "lineWidth": 0,
            "stacking": { "mode": "normal", "group": "A" }
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "answered to caller" },
            "properties": [
              { "id": "custom.stacking", "value": { "mode": "none" } },
              { "id": "custom.drawStyle", "value": "line" },
              { "id": "custom.lineWidth", "value": 3 },
              { "id": "custom.fillOpacity", "value": 0 },
              { "id": "color", "value": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "text" } }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (provider) (rate(gateway_requests_total[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(rate(gateway_responses_total{route=\"/v1/chat/completions\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "answered to caller"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "state-timeline",
      "title": "Circuit state",
      "description": "The money panel. Scoped to the gateway job on purpose: the circuit itself lives in Redis and both processes export their own reading of it, but the worker only re-reads when it happens to route a job, so an idle queue leaves its gauge frozen at whatever it last saw. Aggregating the two - max() especially - lets that stale value outvote the live one and paints a provider OPEN while it is visibly serving traffic. Two views of one fact, so take the one that is continuously refreshed. (This is not the sum-across-jobs rule the request counters need: those count genuinely different work.)",
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 8, "x": 16, "y": 0 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": { "lineWidth": 0, "fillOpacity": 90 },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": { "text": "CLOSED", "color": "green", "index": 0 },
                "1": { "text": "OPEN", "color": "red", "index": 1 },
                "2": { "text": "HALF-OPEN", "color": "orange", "index": 2 }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "mergeValues": true,
        "showValue": "never",
        "alignValue": "left",
        "rowHeight": 0.9,
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "gateway_circuit_state{job=\"gateway\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Errors by provider and type",
      "description": "Only trippable outcomes count against a provider's health. content_filter and bad_request are the caller's fault and never open a circuit; auth and model_not_found are the gateway's own configuration and do.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 9 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "fillOpacity": 20, "lineWidth": 2 }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (provider, error_type) (rate(gateway_provider_errors_total[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}} {{error_type}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "p95 latency by provider",
      "description": "Latency budgets are per provider, not global: groq 5s, anthropic 15s, ollama 60s. Ollama genuinely takes ~14s on local CPU, so one global budget would hold its breaker permanently open and take the floor out of every ladder. The threshold line is drawn at anthropic's 15s, the provider the demo degrades.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 9 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "thresholdsStyle": { "mode": "line" }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 15 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (provider, le) (rate(gateway_request_duration_seconds_bucket[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Failover hops",
      "description": "Each hop names both ends and why it happened. A hop to \"none\" is the ladder running out.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 17 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 60,
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "stacking": { "mode": "normal", "group": "A" }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (from, to, reason) (increase(gateway_failovers_total[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{from}} -> {{to}} ({{reason}})"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Hedging: fired, won, wasted",
      "description": "Hedging roughly doubles spend on the calls it fires, so it is priced honestly here. \"won_by_hedge\" means the second call produced the answer - a hedge that merely returned first, with a failure, counts as wasted.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 17 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "bars", "fillOpacity": 60, "lineWidth": 1 }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (increase(gateway_hedge_total[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queue depth",
      "description": "Deferrable work accepted with a 202 and not yet drained. This climbs when every provider is gone and falls as capacity returns - the outage the queue exists to survive, as a shape.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 8, "x": 0, "y": 25 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "fillOpacity": 30, "lineWidth": 2 }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": false },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "single", "sort": "none" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(gateway_queue_depth)",
          "legendFormat": "queued"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Mean job age, by how it ended",
      "description": "Enqueue to terminal state. \"dead\" is work that survived an outage and still ran out of attempts - the only status that reaches /admin/dlq. \"failed\" is input a provider was right to reject and was never retried. Mean rather than p95: a demo drains single-digit numbers of jobs, and histogram_quantile over a rate window reads NaN unless buckets are still moving - a blank panel exactly when somebody looks at it.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 8, "x": 8, "y": 25 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "fillOpacity": 0, "lineWidth": 2 }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (status) (gateway_job_age_seconds_sum) / sum by (status) (gateway_job_age_seconds_count)",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Spend per hour, by tenant and feature",
      "description": "Why the tenant and feature headers are mandatory at the boundary: cost that cannot be attributed to whoever caused it is cost nobody can act on, and retrofitting required fields onto a live gateway is the migration nobody wants.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 8, "x": 16, "y": 25 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "currencyUSD",
          "decimals": 4,
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 60,
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "stacking": { "mode": "normal", "group": "A" }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (tenant, feature) (rate(gateway_cost_usd_total[5m])) * 3600",
          "legendFormat": "{{tenant}} / {{feature}}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
